.TH PSMatrixFlatten 3 2024-03-09 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSMatrixFlatten\fR

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSMatrixFlatten\fR(\fIPSMatrix matrix\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new matrix that is the single-dimensioned, flatten version of \fImatrix\fR.
.br
For example, if \fImatrix\fR has a shape of (2,3), the resulting matrix will have a shape of (6).  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The new flatten matrix or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fImatrix\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] Memory connot be allocated.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
